Charlie-Bug Codex notes

Project shape:
- Single-page canvas game in index.html.
- No build step, no package manager, no framework.
- JS files load directly in this order: js/data.js, js/draw.js, js/game.js, js/ui.js.

Core files:
- js/data.js: world size, themes, decorations, scatter zones.
- js/draw.js: all canvas drawing, including world art, Charlie, cosmetics, items, particles, celebration.
- js/game.js: state, input, loop, camera, audio, collection, save/resume.
- js/ui.js: celebration mini-canvas and screen-reader announcements.

Current game state:
- Themes are five-piece dress-up sets with hat, wings, antennae, body, and dress slots.
- Role themes include Royal Princess, Firefighter, Wizard, Astronaut, Chef, Artist, Princess Nova, Princess Aurora, and Princess Flora.
- Charlie starts at the tower, collects all five pieces, then must return to the tower before celebration.
- World moods are randomized and saved per day: Spring, Summer, Autumn, Winter, and Moonlight. They palette-swap grass, paths, decorations, ponds, tree canopies, flowers, and overlays.
- Nova, Aurora, and Flora have special world layers: Nova sky, Aurora snowflakes, and Flora bloom overlay.
- Collectibles have larger pickup radius, proximity excitement scaling, item-colored inner glow, white sparkle dots, name cards, and off-screen guide arrows.
- Touch players can tap to walk, with a target ripple. Keyboard, joystick, or gamepad input clears the tap target.
- Charlie has idle look-around, blinking, a dizzy-spin gag after three full turns, and dress rendering.
- Walking leaves fading footprints. Collection triggers a small screen shake, particles, float text, and a capped name-card flash.
- Celebration is full-canvas confetti with spinning Charlie and star rings. The DOM overlay is transparent and only keeps Play Again controls visible.
- Ambient Web Audio music starts once on first user interaction and uses audio-time lookahead scheduling. Mute button is in the HUD.
- itch.io embed prep is in place: metadata, responsive 100svh canvas, iframe border reset, loading screen removed at init.

Persistence:
- Saves use localStorage key charlie-bug-day.
- Storage access is wrapped so sandboxed iframes or blocked localStorage do not crash the game.
- Corrupt or completed saves are cleared.

Recent verification:
- node --check js/data.js
- node --check js/draw.js
- node --check js/game.js
- git diff --check
- headless Chrome file load

Important local rules:
- Keep it single-file HTML plus plain script files. No build step.
- Use textContent or DOM methods for user-facing dynamic text. No innerHTML for user-supplied data.
- Update ../SYNC.md after meaningful changes.
